1dq4|n|a diphthong, employed in the Latin language, and thence in the English language, as the representative of the Greek diphthong oi. In many words in common use, e alone stands instead of /. Classicists prefer to write the diphthong oe separate in Latin words.	v:1dq4,112,2;1tuh,17,3~1tuh,17,3;1dq4,112,2	V:1dq4,112,2~1dq4,112,2	n:1dq4,122,4;tun,38,4;hjx,27,3~tun,38,4;1dq4,122,4;hjx,27,3	N:1dq4,122,4;1iym,53,6;1249,4,2~1iym,53,6;1dq4,122,4;1249,4,2
